    Previously, the `JTSequence` macro-instruction contained a conditional
    branch for the default (selector greater than table size) case. This
    default branch on aarch64 has a +/- 1MiB range. The `JTSequence` also
    contains the entire table of 32-bit offsets for each `br_table`
    target. As a result of these two facts, a branch may have an
    out-of-bounds target and silently wrap the offset, resulting in an
    incorrect branch target.
    
