    wasi-http(p3): tie outbound I/O task lifetime to the store (#14743)
    
    The task driving an outbound request's connection was kept alive by
    three references: the transmission future, the response body and the
    request body. The request body reference is circular in the default
    `send_request` implementation, since the request body is owned by the
    hyper connection that the task itself drives. A guest could therefore
    leave connections running after the store was dropped, with no way for
    the embedder to reclaim them, e.g. by feeding an endless upstream
    response body into another outbound request.
    
    Drop the request and transmission future references and instead have
    the store hold a reference to the task until it finishes. Dropping the
    store now cancels every outbound connection not referenced by something
    the embedder holds, while a response body handed to the host unchanged
    keeps its connection alive for as long as the host reads it.
    
    As a consequence, the guest dropping all of its handles no longer
    cancels the task; it runs until it finishes or the store is dropped.
    
    Assisted-by: claude:claude-fable-5-1
    Assisted-by: claude:claude-opus-5-5

