    Don't instantiate concurrent hostcall glue for non-concurrent host functions (#14517)
    
    `HostFn::run` returned `HostResult<R>`, an enum with a `Future` variant, so
    `call_sync_lower` and `call_async_lower` always contained the arms calling
    `concurrent::poll_and_block` and `Instance::first_poll`. Those methods are
    monomorphized per host closure, which means every `func_wrap`,
    `func_wrap_async`, `func_new` and `func_new_async` host function compiled its
    own copy of the future-handling path even though only the `*_concurrent`
    constructors can produce a future.
    
    Replace the enum with a `HostOutput<R>` trait implemented for `Result<R>` and
    for the boxed future, and select it through an associated `Output` type on
    `HostFn`. Only the future impl references `poll_and_block`/`first_poll`, so
    they are now instantiated only for concurrent host functions. Behavior and
    the public API are unchanged.
    
    For an embedder with ~2,000 `bindgen!`-generated `func_wrap_async` imports
    (fat LTO, codegen-units = 1) this reduces the embedder crate's LLVM IR from
    23.4M to 17.8M lines (-24%), the final link's peak RSS from 18.6 GB to
    16.4 GB, and the release binary from 112.5 MB to 101.2 MB. Component
    wasm-to-host call benchmarks in `benches/call.rs` are unchanged within noise.
    
    Co-authored-by: kkovalchick <kkovalchick@anduril.com>

