    Fix stack map entries for values live across a `try_call` (#14478)
    
    * cranelift-frontend: keep try_call edge args live across the call and reload them afterward
    
    Block-call arguments on a try_call's outgoing edges (normal-return or
    exception-handler) are passed to the successor only after the callee
    returns or unwinds, so they are live across the call. The safepoint
    liveness analysis treated them as uses *at* the call, so they were
    missing from its stack map. A GC during the call could then free or
    move an object that is still in use.
    
    This PR fixes the liveness analysis to process uses in three steps when
    walking backward over each instruction: first block-call arguments; then
    record the safepoint, if there is one; then all other uses (ordinary
    arguments).
    
    It also fixes the rewrite: a spilled value passed on a try_call edge
    must be reloaded *after* the call. When such an edge needs a reload,
    split it with a landing block that reloads the value and then jumps to
    the original target.
    
    * Reject gc-ref context entries in exception tables.
    
