    This patch implements a bubble-semantics for propagating traps through
    nested continuation stacks. Every trap in a continuation is now caught
    by its parent stack, which re-raises the trap to tis parent until the
    trap is ultimately caught by the nearest delimiting host/engine
    frame. In order for this bubbling to correct, we now need to record
    the trap-handler state of each continuation stack such that it can be
    restored accordingly before propagating the trap.
    
