    out of sync if the func is mutated after the CFG's construction.
    
    * Cranelift: compute post-dominator tree lazily
    
    The post-dominator tree is only consulted by dead-store elimination, and only
    for candidates whose two stores live in different blocks (because we can easily
    test post-domination without building a post-dominator tree when the two
    instructions are in the same block). The majority of functions have no such
    dead-store candidates, so building it eagerly for every function is a waste.
    
