    This commit replaces the parallel `observed_regions: EntitySet<AliasRegion>`
    with an `observed` boolean stored inline in each region's state. This removes a
    second heap allocation from every non-empty `LastStores` clone, which happens
    $O(blocks)$ times per function during the block-input fixpoint, and collapses
    `meet_from`'s per-region work into one pass.
    
    * Cranelift: avoid re-fetching opcode in alias_regions_observed
    
    The DSE alias-analysis `update` already has the instruction's opcode; pass it
    into `alias_regions_observed` instead of re-reading it from the DFG, since LLVM
    doesn't seem to dedupe it, and this code runs for every non-memory instruction
    on both the block-input fixpoint and the transform walk.

