    round it down so it is aligned. The previous rounding down only rounded to
    `ALIGN`, which produced a capacity that was an odd multiple of `ALIGN`, which we
    then split in two for each semispace, which meant that each semispace was *not*
    aligned to `ALIGN` (only aligned to `ALIGN/2`). The fix is to round down to the
    next multiple of `2*ALIGN`.

