    Enable reflecting most `Config` values through `Engine` (#13671)
    
    * Enable reflecting most `Config` values through `Engine`
    
    This commit adds a number of pieces of plumbing/etc where the end goal
    is to be able to reflect upon the configuration values from an `Engine`.
    The pieces added here are:
    
    * Many new `get_*` methods now exist on `Engine` to read out the
      configuration values specified. These are intended to not return an
      `Option<T>` in most cases to accurately reflect Wasmtime's defaults
      and configuration.
    
    * The `wasmtime-cli-flags` is now feature'd to have a separate `clap`,
      `serde`, and `toml` feature.
    
    * The `wasmtime-cli-flags` crate structures now sport a `Serialize`
      implementation to go along with their `Deserialize` implementation.
    
    * A new `wasmtime_cli_flags::CommonOptions::from_engine` method was
      added to extract configuration from an `Engine`.
    
    The intent here is that all raw getters are present on `Engine` itself,
    not `Config`. This is an intentional decision as `Config` is a part-way
    piece of configuration which doesn't necessarily have all defaults/etc
    loaded to determine the true final configuration options. An `Engine`,
    however, is a finalized piece of configuration which has a finalized
    `Tunables`, for example.
    
    Additionally `Engine` has accessors based on `Config` names, but it's
    also easy to forget to add these over time. Additionally everything's
    not in a nicely serializable format, but that's what `CommonOptions`
    packages up nicely. The `from_engine` method bridges this gap by
    connecting all `Engine` options to an exhaustive construction of all CLI
    options. This means that if we forget to add one in the future we'll at
    least get a compiler error to alert us.
    
    The overall goal with this is to assist with embeddings updating
    `wasmtime` over time. It should now be much easier to serialize
    Wasmtime's default configuration to a file and persist that across major
    Wasmtime versions. This enables embeddings to configure modules
    uniformly over time and have at least mostly similar settings across
    versions of Wasmtime.
    
    I'll note as well that `from_engine` is not exhaustive. There are
    configuration options that fundamentally can't be captured in a
    serializable format, such a `MemoryCreator` (a trait object). This is
    documented on `from_engine` where it's intended to represent a major
    subset of configuration but not exhaustive. This is suitable for
    applications, though, which exclusively derive a `Config` from
    `CommonOptions` (or similar) where it can be understood that everything
    is still serializable there.
    
