Author: Chris Fallin <chris@cfallin.org>
Date:   Thu May 11 14:30:25 2023 -0700

    Allow a preloaded module to be used by the wizened module.
    
    This PR adds a `--preload` option to Wizer that allows the user to
    provide a second module (in addition to the module being snapshotted)
    whose exprts are available for import by the snapshotted module.
    
    The preloaded module is not snapshotted, and is not linked or included
    in any way into the snapshot. Rather, it is assumed to contain
    intrinsics, stubs, helpers, or other stateless functions that are needed
    by the snapshotted module and that will also be available in its
    post-snapshot execution environment.
    
    This option is useful for, e.g., implementing "intrinsics" for other
    Wasm-transform tools that are implemented as magic imports. These
    imports can be stubbed out during snapshotting, but preserved as calls
    to imports in the snapshot, to enable further processing.

