    `wiggle` dependency and the rights system, and adds a few structs and fields
    specific to Preview 2.  Further changes will follow as we implement more
    features.
    
    The intention is that this version of `wasi-common` will be merged back into
    `wasmtime` and be used there for both the Preview 1 and Preview 2 WASI host
    implementations.  In addition, we would like it to remain runtime-agnostic
    (i.e. not depend on `wasmtime` directly or indirectly) so it can be reused by
    other runtimes, which was the original intention behind `wasi-common`.
